#CHLOEAI:1
TYPE="path_rules"
GLOB="ai_context/**, ai_modules/**, readme_AI.chloeai, AI_HANDOFF.chloeai, WORKSHEET.heywy"

PURPOSE:
Rules active when editing AI context files. Loaded on demand — not every session.
These rules protect continuity integrity.

---

IMMUTABLE_RULES:
- Do not rewrite history in any .chloeai or .heywy file. Append only.
- Do not modify USAGE or header sections of readme_AI.chloeai unless explicitly instructed.
- Do not delete entries from AI_HANDOFF.chloeai — move to HANDOFF_ARCHIVE section if needed.
- Do not delete entries from ai_context/decision_log.md — mark SUPERSEDED instead.
- Closed THREADS move to ai_context/readme_AI_archive.chloeai, not deleted.

WRITEBACK_TARGETS:
- Project state changes → ai_context/current_state.md
- Decisions made → ai_context/decision_log.md + ai_context/readme_AI_archive.chloeai DECISIONS
- Session end → AI_HANDOFF.chloeai (append new entry)
- Human input handled → WORKSHEET.heywy (move to HISTORY section)
- HANDOFF overflow → move oldest from readme_AI.chloeai to ai_context/readme_AI_archive.chloeai

FILE_TYPE_REMINDER:
- .chloeai: AI-facing. Human should not need to read these.
- .heywy: Human-facing. AI reads but does not own the content direction.
